ents of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =1\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271316bb-de9b-5d8b-bad0-ffd1bfc5b101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420447} {:answer/id #uuid "633d97e3-8d84-57c9-8ac7-bdd2378d9d50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420449} {:answer/id #uuid "c2051bdd-22cb-509c-8fb6-340e90eb858d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420456} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4325a-2b33-5c98-a020-248e21f996f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420459} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d19e05-07c5-5adc-9a1c-131ee586eacd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271316bb-de9b-5d8b-bad0-ffd1bfc5b101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420447} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f94aaa-a8cf-5aa4-9f93-884e35c10a15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420464}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b667d36f-710b-5326-b636-9597ec1ec3f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-77230" :question/problem "![](images/8c/8cf7d0520b1d0654d5749651595acd48b7a08f2b2d55142b18ca63b2ded20f55.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+2b$, find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/9e/9edea1e3ad727d11d7bfac884f27c1b435233fa7df561dbe2a4f3af45ea16bfa.png)\n\nIn $△OBC$, we have:\n\n- $BC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{BC}=3a.$ \n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}+\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & =2b+3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=2b+\\lambda a=2b+3a.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =3\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Scalar Factor in a Linear Combination"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096447 :question/id #uuid "2a61b115-4e26-5966-b2a9-d2fedef6b728" :question/math-academy-id "e-4282" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ has magnitude $3$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$." :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$, we divide $\\mathbf{a}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=\\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be1529be-a7de-5974-b991-d60dde835856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093789} {:answer/id #uuid "d540dace-2707-5500-b5c4-ab774e31fbd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093790} {:answer/id #uuid "03b0e61c-7ea0-5634-9db6-b0e0196b04fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093791} {:answer/id #uuid "40cede01-8d57-5e23-8ad3-1718dcad0ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093792} {:answer/id #uuid "6da8d0ca-8218-54d1-b8e7-7f100838a138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093793}] :answer-field/id #uuid "45156f70-5185-5291-966e-5fa7eea23fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093788}] :question/id #uuid "b156a92a-15b2-528d-ba13-ee9f57edd97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-11376" :question/problem "The vector $a$ has magnitude $5$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf21b48-ac6a-5eb5-baae-9633dd304e0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "AB^(→)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094244} {:answer/id #uuid "977b610a-551c-59f5-84f0-c040fca5dc39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7BA^(→)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094245} {:answer/id #uuid "a82e8ce4-1708-5923-88f5-d53ecb21f727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-AB^(→)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094246} {:answer/id #uuid "5a30ca90-e143-59b7-bc1e-3db89f4da91d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}AB^(→)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094247} {:answer/id #uuid "6e9a9def-4be8-5d8d-829a-14522ce6c590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7BA^(→)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094248}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ffccd89c-0549-5a01-82df-21cfa90868da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094243}] :question/id #uuid "69f15d42-ddf8-532a-8779-b147d80f8a1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-12202" :question/problem "The vector $AB^(→)$ has magnitude $7$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $AB^(→)$?"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096493 :question/id #uuid "6dfe09f0-30e2-53bc-a8f6-d7e4a3b8232a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5181" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3042242136b82b867b8bd7911761ee38318924df0c9979488d20f04117c45d9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf a$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b3/b316448c885a20a7ed60871ce0f1a4dc4f77bd4658dc6eda3407fb3c89a088cb.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\n, $AH=3$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^{2} + BH^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$ is $\\sqrt{13}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{\\mid a \\mid} \\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae96c78f-e10d-563b-82af-e2c02160928e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094940} {:answer/id #uuid "25f7a90e-939a-568d-ba3d-07a616fcb021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094941} {:answer/id #uuid "328e6ad2-ef2f-5827-8881-60cdfaebb76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2q}{\\sqrt{13}} + \\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094942} {:answer/id #uuid "681555fa-cdb3-5281-b943-0cf1eed80c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(q + r))/(\\sqrt{73})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094943} {:answer/id #uuid "703e463a-8826-5adf-9d3d-36bfd8037d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094944}] :answer-field/id #uuid "96962338-e491-50f7-b8da-1efc8b69ba83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094939}] :question/id #uuid "9d05ca0e-131b-5294-8367-1760396e4369" :question/math-academy-id "q-19276" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dfaf74a497a2fd22428e09a4c26d573e184c9728ccf67f11ebb9d6a2a44f4c6.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $q + r$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8688d259-91a0-57b9-a118-ec71feec2112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095036} {:answer/id #uuid "a1324d04-e706-5a76-a501-88a91adb3e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{55}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095037} {:answer/id #uuid "228bdee3-07e5-5a7d-9a23-1d3da2c66da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095038} {:answer/id #uuid "44ddca2e-c35f-567f-9191-68cb552e7650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{55}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095039} {:answer/id #uuid "4741a424-03b7-5a24-97e3-1e5c43226795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{65}}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095040}] :answer-field/id #uuid "943eaa96-2961-5fec-9654-295f42c3d887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095035}] :question/id #uuid "8ddbfd9c-fd49-551e-8c5c-9bdbb0fc04fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-20407" :question/problem "![](images/13/1319298a994d5daf26853baf7d255490827ada4123debdf0b4374db1ed03f7af.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233276 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45f48cf6-e519-5407-abc6-4bbd59c8789a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119805" :question/problem "![](images/95/95c30eab094a24beb6976262167401efa973dbac12781c69d074eb14e12e2743.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n:$ \n\n![](images/87/87647211f77776c5f5f740c205fafb150eef1b9d3ebefb82df73a9fdcd953bdb.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=0.5=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $BH=2.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|m+n| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}(m+n).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096448 :question/id #uuid "23d9a601-974b-51c2-a6ea-0ebadde19efc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4283" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $10$, while the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $20$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a+b}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $\\mathbf{a+b}$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ goes from the tail of $\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n![](images/32/32c48d8c19fc68fbc172b240ded922f3e2ebc12804411c318ff63fe999aaedcc.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $\\mathbf{a+b}$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a + b & ^{2} &= & a & ^{2} +\\left.\\end{vmatrix}b\\right|^{2} \\\\\n&= 10^{2} + 20^{2} \\\\\n&= 100 + 400 \\\\\n&= 500\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\mathbf{a+b} &= \\sqrt{500}=10\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10\\sqrt{5}}(a + b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44ac67b-5e3d-5b1e-bf2c-554b592ba29e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab0413fa-4042-5147-a3d8-818097bc2626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094226} {:answer/id #uuid "c81ea504-05ac-5c44-a92e-1630193abb8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094227} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b9b147-1585-55ec-b881-e10cd196e800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094228} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5dad94-0917-544d-85f3-4e70f0e93daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094229} {:answer/id #uuid "24b28af8-0f33-5293-a88e-61ee2a659e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094230}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bd239bbe-a8f9-5077-a835-d71f38e1b449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094225}] :question/id #uuid "3f0752f9-cfba-5496-a6dc-d603b64b1e81" :question/math-academy-id "q-12184" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $3$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $4$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097043 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c27fb23c-7e75-5962-96da-f5d4cdf55baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{569}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094232} {:answer/id #uuid "e7540039-cc90-5f35-b9e5-f11de4ba13e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{573}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094233} {:answer/id #uuid "2d97d629-615d-5343-ae83-2b49d9c22d39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{561}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094234} {:answer/id #uuid "3938b713-9ab0-5b89-b60b-79de69627c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{23}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094235} {:answer/id #uuid "521a0f0f-f648-5c38-afda-9cbb447db899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094236}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5e4bfff2-68a6-59a4-831d-e2298ec06fa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094231}] :question/id #uuid "d188cb86-3193-5752-99d0-e273954248f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-12185" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $\\mid a|= 20$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-east and $\\mid b|= 13$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"}]}
